@alextran1502 That's right. Nginx within `immich-proxy` should directly serve the web page assets. nginx config (shortened) would look something like this:
```
server {
  location /api {
    proxy_pass http://immich-server:3001;
  }
  location / {
    root   /path/to/html/and/js/files;
    try_files $uri $uri/index.html $uri.html /index.html;
    index  index.html index.htm;
  }
}
```

SvelteKit has an [adapter](https://kit.svelte.dev/docs/adapters#supported-environments-static-sites) `@sveltejs/adapter-static` for static sites. Maybe the `try_files` in the nginx config needs some tweaking to make routing and direct links work etc.

I think what you will want to do is something similar to the setup below.


```nginx
server {
  listen       80;
  server_name  immich.mydoamin.com;

  location / {
    proxy_pass  http://your-local-machine-ip-running-immich:2283;
  }
}
```

